b. Advisor;  
c. Coordinator;  
d. Chairperson;  
e. Vice Chairpersonf. Secretary;  
g. Vice Secretary;  
h. Treasurer; andi. Members.  
2. Coordinators consist of:a. Assistance and Advocacy Division;  
b. Service and Recovery Division;  
c. Network and Information Strengthening Division;  
d. Education and Training Division;  
e. Case Manager; andf. Expert Team.  
3. Further provisions regarding the organizational structure of P2TP2A and description of coordinator duties are further regulated by Regent Regulation.

#### Article 12

P2TP2A builds functional networks with: a. Police;  
b. Prosecutor's Office;  
c. Court;  
d. Hospital/Community Health Center;  
e. Psychiatrist; and - 12 -f. Other institutions that have common goals.

#### Article 13

P2TP2A as an independent institution in the region must be in one coordination with the SKPD whose scope of duties and responsibilities includes the field of Women's Empowerment and Regional Child Protection.

## Part Three

Financing of P2TP2A

#### Article 14

1. The Government assists the operations of P2TP2A by budgeting in the APBD in accordance with the capacity and financial condition of the region.  
2. Budgeting as referred to in paragraph (1) is through the SKPD whose scope of duties and responsibilities includes the field of Women's Empowerment and Regional Child Protection.  
3. For orderly administration and use of P2TP2A finances, it is obliged to make work programs and accountability for the use of regional finances.

#### Article 15

1. P2TP2A financing in addition to being obtained from APBD funds can be through obtaining assistance receipts from individuals, bodies, or official institutions whose existence is legally recognized.  
2. P2TP2A is obliged to submit annual reports for performance and financial receipts from the APBD to the Regent through the SKPD whose scope of duties and responsibilities includes the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the Region.

# CHAPTER VII

## PREVENTION, SERVICES AND EMPOWERMENT

## Part One

General

#### Article 16

The Regional Government through the regional P2TP2A, carries out prevention and service efforts for victims of violence, exploitation and neglect of Children and Women up to the empowerment of victims to be able to return to living their lives in accordance with the dignity they possess.  

