## Part Three

Services for Women and Children Experiencing Acts of Violence, Exploitation and Neglect

#### Article 18

1. The form of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence, exploitation, trafficking in persons or neglect is implemented in accordance with the rights of victims as referred to in Article 4 paragraph (2) and paragraph (3).  
2. To support the operations of P2TP2A, the Regent orders the SKPD related to services as referred to in paragraph (1) in accordance with minimum service standards established by the government.

#### Article 19

The Regional Government or P2TP2A is obliged to establish operational standards for Assistance to victims of violence, exploitation, trafficking or neglect in every stage of fulfilling the rights of victims.

#### Article 20

The implementation of services and assistance to victims is carried out with the principles of:
a. non-discrimination;  
b. fast, safe, and empathetic;  
c. coordination between government agencies;  
d. guarantee of confidentiality;  
e. easily accessible; andf. no fees charged.

## Part Four

Empowerment of Victims of Acts of Violence

#### Article 21

1. The Regional Government through P2TP2A is obliged to carry out economic empowerment of victims of acts of violence, exploitation and/or trafficking or neglect.  
2. The form of empowerment of victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:a. providing the necessary needs for entrepreneurship training for victims of acts of violence, in order to increase knowledge, attitudes, and business skills;  
b. facilitating the implementation of various job training and skills training;  

15 -
c. providing assistance in developing productive economic businesses;  
d. exploring cooperation with small, medium and large companies, as well as financial institutions to develop businesses of victims of acts of violence;  
e. seeking the provision of capital for victims of acts of violence; andf. expanding access to information and promoting the products of victims of acts of violence.

# CHAPTER VIII

## COOPERATION AND PARTNERSHIP

## Part One

Cooperation

#### Article 22

1. Cooperation is carried out to strengthen the role of P2TP2A in achieving the objectives of protecting women and children in the regional area.  
2. Cooperation is carried out with:a. the government;  
b. the provincial government;  
c. other regency/city governments;  
d. non-governmental institutions; ande. international institutions whose existence is recognized.  
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (2), includes:a. exchange of data and information;  
b. rehabilitation of victims of acts of violence;  
c. repatriation and social reintegration; andd. provision of evidence and witnesses, and followed up based on the provisions of laws and regulations.  
4. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), is set forth in the form of a joint agreement.

## Part Two

Partnership

#### Article 23

1. The Regional Government establishes partnerships with the business world to support the implementation of protection for women and children in the regional area.  
2. Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out through: - 16 -a. notification of information on employment opportunities for women victims of acts of violence;  
b. education and training for women victims of acts of violence;  
c. educational assistance for women and children victims of acts of violence who have been withdrawn from their education; andd. fostering and increasing the economic independence of women victims of acts of violence.  
3. Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), is set forth in the form of an agreement.

# CHAPTER IX

## COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION

#### Article 24

1. In implementing protection for women and children, the community can:a. form family partners at the village/sub-district level by the community;  
b. form women and children protection units within community organizations;  
c. conduct socialization of women's and children's rights independently;  
d. provide first aid to victims; ande. report to the competent authority if violence against victims occurs in their environment.  
2. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, the private sector, and mass media.

# CHAPTER X

## REGIONAL ACTION PLAN

#### Article 25

1. In order to carry out obligations and responsibilities, the regional government establishes programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in 1 (one) RAD as the basis for implementing protection for women and children from acts of violence.  
2. RAD as referred to in paragraph (1), is part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).  

17 - (3) Further provisions regarding RAD as referred to in paragraph (1), are regulated by Regent Regulation.

# CHAPTER IX

## GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

#### Article 26

1. The Regent conducts guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.  
2. The Regent may appoint the Head of SKPD whose scope of duties and responsibilities includes the protection of women and children to conduct guidance and supervision.

#### Article 27

The community may conduct supervision over the implementation of protection of women and children in the regional area with a mechanism for conveying aspirations to the Regent or DPRD.
